            <div xml:id="d460">

                <pb facs="0545" n="457" xml:id="pg457"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/1022: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-06T14:00:00+01:00">February 6, 1933—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 6—1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>94. Drummond tells me that his latest information is to the effect that Peru has
                    rejected the Brazilian proposals; that Brazilian mediation has come to an end
                    and that an armed clash seems likely between Peruvian and Colombian forces on
                    the latter’s territory. He adds that situation may momentarily become serious
                    and cooperation of great importance. He would much appreciate any information
                    you have tending to confirm or refute these reports.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
